# Hello, C

A C program is compiled to machine code before it runs. Every program starts in `main`, and what `main` returns is the program's exit status:

```c
#include <stdio.h>

int main(void) {
    puts("Hello, C");
    return 0;
}
```

`puts` writes a string and a newline to standard output. Returning 0 tells the shell that all went well.

